        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Find <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\left|z\\right|]</span> if <span class=\"math\">[MATH: z=3 - 4\\textrm{i}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Find [MATH: \\left|z\\right|] if [MATH: z=3 - 4\\textrm{i}.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>For a complex number <span class=\"math\">[MATH: z=a+b\\textrm{i},]</span> the magnitude of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: z]</span> is given by\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: |z| = \\sqrt{a^2+b^2} .]</span></p><p>For the complex number <span class=\"math\">[MATH: z=3-4\\textrm{i},]</span> we have <span class=\"math\">[MATH: a=3]</span> and <span class=\"math\">[MATH: b=-4.]</span> So, the magnitude is given by</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: |z||= sqrt((3)^{2} + (\u2212 4)^{2}); = sqrt(9 + 16); = sqrt(25); = 5.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "For a complex number [MATH: z=a+b\\textrm{i},] the magnitude of [MATH: z] is given by\n[MATH: |z| = \\sqrt{a^2+b^2} .]\n\nFor the complex number [MATH: z=3-4\\textrm{i},] we have [MATH: a=3] and [MATH: b=-4.] So, the magnitude is given by\n\n[MATH: |z||= sqrt((3)^{2} + (\u2212 4)^{2}); = sqrt(9 + 16); = sqrt(25); = 5.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nFind [MATH: \\left|z\\right|] if [MATH: z=3 - 4\\textrm{i}.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFor a complex number [MATH: z=a+b\\textrm{i},] the magnitude of [MATH: z] is given by\n[MATH: |z| = \\sqrt{a^2+b^2} .]\n\nFor the complex number [MATH: z=3-4\\textrm{i},] we have [MATH: a=3] and [MATH: b=-4.] So, the magnitude is given by\n\n[MATH: |z||= sqrt((3)^{2} + (\u2212 4)^{2}); = sqrt(9 + 16); = sqrt(25); = 5.]"
      },
