        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>What is the magnitude of the number <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\textrm{i}\\sqrt{2}?]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "What is the magnitude of the number [MATH: \\textrm{i}\\sqrt{2}?]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>The imaginary number <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\textrm{i} \\sqrt{2}]</span> is equivalent to the complex number <span class=\"math\">[MATH: z = 0 + \\sqrt{2} \\textrm{i}.]</span></p><p>We know that for a complex number <span class=\"math\">[MATH: z=a+b\\textrm{i},]</span> the magnitude of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: z]</span> is given by\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: |z| = \\sqrt{a^2+b^2} .]</span></p><p>So, its magnitude of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: z=0 + \\sqrt{2} \\textrm{i}]</span> is given by\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: |z||= sqrt(a^{2} + b^{2}); = sqrt((0)^{2} + (sqrt(2))^{2}); = sqrt(0 + 2); = sqrt(2).]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "The imaginary number [MATH: \\textrm{i} \\sqrt{2}] is equivalent to the complex number [MATH: z = 0 + \\sqrt{2} \\textrm{i}.]\n\nWe know that for a complex number [MATH: z=a+b\\textrm{i},] the magnitude of [MATH: z] is given by\n[MATH: |z| = \\sqrt{a^2+b^2} .]\n\nSo, its magnitude of [MATH: z=0 + \\sqrt{2} \\textrm{i}] is given by\n[MATH: |z||= sqrt(a^{2} + b^{2}); = sqrt((0)^{2} + (sqrt(2))^{2}); = sqrt(0 + 2); = sqrt(2).]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nWhat is the magnitude of the number [MATH: \\textrm{i}\\sqrt{2}?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nThe imaginary number [MATH: \\textrm{i} \\sqrt{2}] is equivalent to the complex number [MATH: z = 0 + \\sqrt{2} \\textrm{i}.]\n\nWe know that for a complex number [MATH: z=a+b\\textrm{i},] the magnitude of [MATH: z] is given by\n[MATH: |z| = \\sqrt{a^2+b^2} .]\n\nSo, its magnitude of [MATH: z=0 + \\sqrt{2} \\textrm{i}] is given by\n[MATH: |z||= sqrt(a^{2} + b^{2}); = sqrt((0)^{2} + (sqrt(2))^{2}); = sqrt(0 + 2); = sqrt(2).]"
      },
