          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>For a complex number <span class=\"math\">[MATH: z=a+b\\textrm{i},]</span> the magnitude of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: z]</span> is given by\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: |z| = \\sqrt{a^2+b^2} .]</span></p><p>For the complex number <span class=\"math\">[MATH: z=5c - 9d\\textrm{i},]</span> we have <span class=\"math\">[MATH: a=5c]</span> and <span class=\"math\">[MATH: b=-9d.]</span> So, the magnitude is given by</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: |z||= sqrt((5c)^{2} + (\u2212 9d)^{2}); = sqrt(25c^{2} + 81d^{2}).]</span></p>",
